- @next: A third consecutive victory for Thatcher's Conservatives

@next

Despite miner's strikes, violence in Northern Ireland and economic troubles, Thatcher manages to hold onto her majority despite losing some seats. 

The Labour Party managed to slightly bounce back however the splitting of the anti-conservative vote between them and the SDP–Liberal Alliance made it inevitable that the Conservatives would window
